<div class="space-y-2" aria-label="Attendance colour meanings">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 text-xs font-semibold">
        <span class="rounded-lg border border-sky-100 bg-sky-50 px-3 py-2 text-sky-800">Blue · Weekly shop closed</span>
        <span class="rounded-lg border border-violet-100 bg-violet-50 px-3 py-2 text-violet-800">Purple · Special shop closed</span>
        <span class="rounded-lg border border-amber-100 bg-amber-50 px-3 py-2 text-amber-800">Amber · Paid leave, no absence deduction</span>
        <span class="rounded-lg border border-rose-100 bg-rose-50 px-3 py-2 text-rose-800">Red · Absent / unpaid, normal deduction</span>
        <span class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white px-3 py-2 text-slate-700">White · Other attendance / future rows</span>
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-600"><strong>Not paid leave?</strong> Leave Check In and Check Out blank and uncheck Paid leave. The row becomes red and imports as Absent with the normal absence deduction. If the person worked, enter their actual times instead. Shop closed days are not personal leave.</p>
</div>
